OHOS: draw the window's caption buttons in the tab strip. The shell asks for
titleBarStyle 'hidden' and leaves minimize, maximize/restore and close to the
platform's titleBarOverlay; electron-ohos implements no overlay and its window
decor is all-or-nothing, so a window created that way has no button to close,
maximize or minimize it. The renderer drives the window it lives in through a
small IPC channel instead.

The maximize state is tracked from the window's maximize/unmaximize events
rather than read back through win.isMaximized(): electron-ohos reports a freshly
created window as maximized until its state first changes, which painted the
restore icon on a floating window.

